    {
      "id": "fr-medias-3",
      "title": "Je le regarde",
      "subtitle": "The pronouns le, la, les",
      "topics": [
        "object-pronouns",
        "media"
      ],
      "words": [
        "verbs#to stop"
      ],
      "learn": [
        {
          "title": "le, la, les",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "So that you don't repeat a noun, replace it with *le* (masculine), *la* (feminine) or *les* (plural). Before a vowel it's *l'*. The pronoun goes **before the verb**: *Je regarde la série → Je la regarde.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "textCols": [0],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "I'm watching it. (le film)",
                  "Je le regarde."
                ],
                [
                  "I'm watching it. (la série)",
                  "Je la regarde."
                ],
                [
                  "I'm watching them. (les vidéos)",
                  "Je les regarde."
                ],
                [
                  "I love it. (the show)",
                  "Je l'adore."
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "transform",
                "task_en": "Replace the underlined words with a pronoun",
                "fr": "Je regarde [la télé].",
                "a": [
                  "Je la regarde."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Negatives and infinitives",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "In the negative, *ne ... pas* goes around the pronoun and the verb: *Je ne la regarde pas.* With an infinitive the pronoun goes before the infinitive: *Je vais le regarder ce soir.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "title": "more in Grammar",
              "en": "You'll find every situation step by step in Grammar, in the chapter *Object pronouns step by step*."
            },
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Ton portable ? Je ne le trouve pas.",
                  "en": "Your phone? I can't find it."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Cette appli ? Je l'utilise tous les jours.",
                  "en": "This app? I use it every day."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Les infos ? Je les regarde le soir.",
                  "en": "The news? I watch it in the evening."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Le match ? On va le regarder chez Tom.",
                  "en": "The match? We're going to watch it at Tom's."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "I'll see it tomorrow. (the film)",
                "a": [
                  "Je vais le voir demain.",
                  "Je le vois demain.",
                  "Je le verrai demain."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "vocab"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
