    {
      "id": "fr-medias-4",
      "title": "Je lui envoie un message",
      "subtitle": "The pronouns lui, leur",
      "topics": [
        "object-pronouns"
      ],
      "words": [
        "verbs-irregular#to say, to tell"
      ],
      "learn": [
        {
          "title": "lui and leur",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "When a verb goes with *à* + a person (*envoyer à, écrire à, téléphoner à, répondre à, dire à, parler à*), you replace the person with *lui* (to him or to her) or *leur* (to them)."
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "textCols": [0],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "I'm writing to him.",
                  "Je lui écris."
                ],
                [
                  "I'm writing to her.",
                  "Je lui écris."
                ],
                [
                  "I'm writing to them.",
                  "Je leur écris."
                ],
                [
                  "I'm phoning him.",
                  "Je lui téléphone."
                ],
                [
                  "I'm answering them.",
                  "Je leur réponds."
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "tip",
              "title": "lui = to him and to her",
              "en": "*Lui* works for a man and a woman. And *leur* never takes *-s*."
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "transform",
                "task_en": "Replace the underlined words with a pronoun",
                "fr": "J'écris [à ma grand-mère].",
                "a": [
                  "Je lui écris."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "le or lui?",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "en": "Ask yourself: is there *à* after the verb? Yes → *lui / leur*. No → *le / la / les*. *Je regarde Paul → Je le regarde. Je parle à Paul → Je lui parle.*"
            },
            {
              "type": "examples",
              "items": [
                {
                  "fr": "Mon frère ? Je lui envoie une vidéo.",
                  "en": "My brother? I'm sending him a video."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Mes parents ? Je leur téléphone le soir.",
                  "en": "My parents? I phone them in the evening."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Léa ? Je l'appelle demain.",
                  "en": "Léa? I'll call her tomorrow."
                },
                {
                  "fr": "Tu leur as répondu ?",
                  "en": "Did you answer them?"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "check",
              "item": {
                "type": "build",
                "en": "I'm phoning them.",
                "a": [
                  "Je leur téléphone.",
                  "Je les appelle."
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Words",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "vocab"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "id": "fr-medias-4-01",
